<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    Partial Info.plist that merges with the keys synthesized from
    INFOPLIST_KEY_* build settings (GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE = YES).

    Lives here because nested-array/dictionary keys
    (NSAppTransportSecurity, CFBundleURLTypes) cannot be expressed as
    flat INFOPLIST_KEY_* settings.

    NSAllowsLocalNetworking only relaxes ATS for loopback, .local, and
    RFC1918 private IPs. Public hosts still must speak HTTPS — Release
    builds hit api.tigerduck.app over HTTPS and are unaffected.

    TLS pinning is **not** declared here via `NSPinnedDomains` despite
    that being the natural fit. We tested it (mitmproxy-style
    experiment against a host with deliberately bogus pins) and
    confirmed that `NSPinnedDomains` is enforced at a layer beneath
    `URLSessionDelegate` — even returning `useCredential(URLCredential(
    trust:))` with no pre-check still gets rejected. Apple's ATS pin
    has no fail-soft expiry mechanism, and there is no way for app
    code to bypass a stale-pin rejection. Since issue #92 requires
    fail-soft after the pin set's expiration date (to spare users on
    un-updated builds when TWCA rotates the chain), pinning is done
    programmatically via `TLSPinningDelegate` (swift/Shared/) wired
    onto every URLSession that talks to a pinned host.

    CFBundleURLTypes registers the `tigerduck://` scheme used by the
    widget `widgetURL(...)` deep links (TigerDuckWidgets). Without
    this, WidgetKit has no host to hand the tap to and Library /
    classtable shortcuts silently no-op. Router lives in
    TigerDuckApp.onOpenURL.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>NSAppTransportSecurity</key>
    <dict>
        <key>NSAllowsLocalNetworking</key>
        <true/>
    </dict>
    <key>CFBundleURLTypes</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>CFBundleTypeRole</key>
            <string>Editor</string>
            <key>CFBundleURLName</key>
            <string>org.ntust.app.TigerDuck</string>
            <key>CFBundleURLSchemes</key>
            <array>
                <string>tigerduck</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
